From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:06:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Keep PLL_AUDIO1 at its reset rate

PLL_AUDIO1 has two fixed output taps, DIV2 and DIV5, and the audio
module clocks can take either of them as a parent. Both taps pass rate
requests up to the PLL, so a block on one tap can retune the rate of a
block running on the other.

PLL_AUDIO1 comes out of reset at the manual's 48 kHz point: DIV5 gives
614.4 MHz, which divides to 24.576 MHz (512 x 48 kHz) exactly. Stop
passing rate requests up from the taps, so the PLL stays there and the
taps act as two fixed sources. The 44.1 kHz rates come from PLL_AUDIO0.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; PLL_AUDIO1 reads
0xF1147F00 (N-1 = 0x7f) before and after OWA streams at 48 kHz and at
44.1 kHz.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index be50812f8c16..38cf2bc6afd0 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -408,9 +408,9 @@ static const struct clk_hw *pll_audio1_hws[] = {
 	&pll_audio1_clk.common.hw
 };
 static CLK_FIXED_FACTOR_HWS(pll_audio1_div2_clk, "pll-audio1-div2",
-			    pll_audio1_hws, 2, 1, CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+			    pll_audio1_hws, 2, 1, 0);
 static CLK_FIXED_FACTOR_HWS(pll_audio1_div5_clk, "pll-audio1-div5",
-			    pll_audio1_hws, 5, 1, CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+			    pll_audio1_hws, 5, 1, 0);
 
 #define SUN60I_A733_PLL_NPU_REG		0x2a0
 static struct ccu_nkmp pll_npu_clk = {
